KG42.register("edges-223e82e88b740c4e920c6ffe",{"id":"S-6646138425b9f298","source":"COMP-464efdadf92efbd8","type":"links","target":"COMP-c6ecf48e92525ee2","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["21-dso_flexibility_optimization"],"assertions":[{"id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E004","paper":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","rule_ref":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R003","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E004","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-010"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C005"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-464efdadf92efbd8","target":"COMP-c6ecf48e92525ee2","source_occurrence_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R003::V::coordination.local_operator","target_occurrence_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R003::V::clearing.local","source_unit_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-a-M01::coordination.local_operator","target_unit_id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Availability restrictions on contracted flexibility used in local allocation. | Battery feasibility constraints in local allocation. | Battery terminal-energy restriction in the simulated case study. | Configured operating bounds for curtailable disconnectable loads in local allocation. | Continuity of curtailable disconnectable load schedules in local allocation. | Daily allocation sequence described for the case study. | Directional availability of curtailable disconnectable loads in the allocation model. | Disconnectable-generator feasibility restrictions in local allocation. | Downward-regulation constraints in the local flexibility allocation problem. | Local allocation priorities under the Traffic Light Concept used in the formulation. | Objective of the local flexibility allocation problem. | Reducible-generator feasibility constraints in local allocation. | SESP scheduling of local flexible resources for the operation day. | SESP-operated local flexibility market serving DSO power-quality requirements. | Service scope of the presented local flexibility market. | Shiftable-profile load feasibility in local allocation. | Upward-regulation constraints in the local flexibility allocation problem.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-004","v141-b-g01-ev-006","v141-b-g01-ev-007","v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g01-ev-013","v141-b-g02-ev05","v141-b-g02-ev10","v141-b-g02-ev11","v141-b-g02-ev13","v141-b-g02-ev15","v141-b-g02-ev20","v141-b-g02-ev21","v141-b-g02-ev22","v141-b-g02-ev23","v141-b-g02-ev25","v141-b-g02-ev29","v141-b-g02-ev33","v141-b-g02-ev34","v141-b-g02-ev36","v141-b-g02-ev37","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g04-e03"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"bd5c5dfd7abe48481352fb6cfe9319c0fa27c75b4619551ec7d1aca4a577a7a3","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The SESP, acting as aggregator, receives DSO flexibility requests specifying minimum active-energy variations relative to the forecast baseline, without knowing grid-status information. Scope: DSO upward- and downward-regulation requests in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. The SESP's coordination of corrective actions must give DSO needs maximum priority to avoid over-voltages or transformer over-loads. Scope: SESP coordination of corrective actions in the local flexibility market. Condition: During a DSO-designated yellow-light grid situation. The SESP may send direct control signals overriding local household energy-management decisions. Scope: SESP control authority over local household resource decisions. Condition: During a grid-constrained yellow-light situation. The SESP's forecast must have DSO approval before it is used as the baseline scenario. Scope: Use of SESP forecasts as the flexibility-market baseline. Condition: When a consumption or generation forecast for a flexible asset is to be used as the baseline scenario.","target_definition":"The DSO's requested flexibility supplies the input for determining local resource allocations over the operation day. Scope: SESP scheduling of local flexible resources for the operation day. The requested upward active-energy variation imposes a minimum on the net upward regulation allocated relative to the forecasted baseline; contributions opposing the request remain included in the constraint. Scope: Upward-regulation constraints in the local flexibility allocation problem. Condition: During upward-regulation periods with a positive DSO request. The requested downward active-energy variation imposes a minimum on the magnitude of net downward regulation allocated relative to the forecasted baseline; contributions opposing the request remain included in the constraint. Scope: Downward-regulation constraints in the local flexibility allocation problem. Condition: During downward-regulation periods with a negative DSO request. The DSO sends its flexibility needs before the SESP executes the daily local allocation algorithm. Scope: Daily allocation sequence described for the case study. The SESP, acting as the local market coordinator, determines which flexible resources are allocated to meet the DSO request. Scope: SESP-operated local flexibility market serving DSO power-quality requirements. Local allocation minimizes the SESP's operating cost of meeting the DSO request over the following periods, using flexibility costs predefined in SESP-community member contracts. Scope: Objective of the local flexibility allocation problem. Local flexibility allocation is restricted to providing flexibility to the DSO. Scope: Service scope of the presented local flexibility market. DSO needs receive maximum priority to avoid over-voltages or transformer over-loads; prosumer or aggregator priorities are not considered. Scope: Local allocation priorities under the Traffic Light Concept used in the formulation. Condition: During yellow light situations. Allocation must respect the contracted times during which the offered flexibility can be used. Scope: Availability restrictions on contracted flexibility used in local allocation. Condition: When allocating resources whose flexibility contracts specify permitted usage times. Allocated generation curtailment is nonnegative and cannot exceed the forecasted generation. Scope: Reducible-generator feasibility constraints in local allocation. Condition: For reducible generators in each scheduling period. Allocation permits only switching these generators on or off; intermediate production setpoints are unavailable. Scope: Disconnectable-generator feasibility restrictions in local allocation. Condition: For disconnectable generators. Battery allocations must respect per-period charging and discharging limits and maximum storage capacity, with charging and discharging efficiencies included in state-of-charge accounting. Scope: Battery feasibility constraints in local allocation. Condition: When allocating battery charging or discharging. The allocation schedule must either maintain the disconnection or reconnect the load in the current period. Scope: Continuity of curtailable disconnectable load schedules in local allocation. Condition: After a load was disconnected or remained disconnected in the preceding period. Allocation schedules must respect the maximum number of disconnection orders per day, the minimum resting time between disconnections and the maximum disconnection duration, as applicable. Scope: Configured operating bounds for curtailable disconnectable loads in local allocation. Condition: When the corresponding disconnection-count, resting-time or duration bounds are specified. Curtailable disconnectable loads cannot supply downward regulation because they cannot consume outside their baseline. Scope: Directional availability of curtailable disconnectable loads in the allocation model. Condition: When allocating downward regulation. The scheduled consumption profile must fit the permitted shifting window. Postponement preserves the consumption profile, cannot split it, and allows only one shift per shifting period. Scope: Shiftable-profile load feasibility in local allocation. Condition: For each appliance and its permitted shifting periods, including when the profile is not postponed. The case-study allocation includes a terminal constraint restoring stored energy to its initial amount at the end of the simulation horizon. Scope: Battery terminal-energy restriction in the simulated case study.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The SESP, acting as the local market coordinator, determines which flexible resources are allocated to meet the DSO request. Scope: SESP-operated local flexibility market serving DSO power-quality requirements.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-010"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-001","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"be In order to run these markets, local traders need the SESP Platform for or sending information, t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A local flexibility market (LFM) is an electricity trading platform to sell and buy flexibility in geographically limited areas like neighbourhoods and small towns. The SESP is the local market platform provider and community aggregator (AGR). At the same time, the SESP is a BRP from the regulatory point of view because it bids in wholesale markets. In order to run these markets, local traders need the SESP Platform for sending information, trading for flexibility, and scheduling actions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-010","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-settlement","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"re e- i- ty ed he Fig. 3. Consumer’s ﬂexibility oﬀers example. ed y- resources sorted from the cheap","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Therefore, according to the DSO requirements to manage power quality issues, the SESP decides which resources are necessary to meet the request and sends the control signals to them. After that, the participants with activated resources are then rewarded based on their flexibility contract."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Availability restrictions on contracted flexibility used in local allocation. | Battery feasibility constraints in local allocation. | Battery terminal-energy restriction in the simulated case study. | Configured operating bounds for curtailable disconnectable loads in local allocation. | Continuity of curtailable disconnectable load schedules in local allocation. | Daily allocation sequence described for the case study. | Directional availability of curtailable disconnectable loads in the allocation model. | Disconnectable-generator feasibility restrictions in local allocation. | Downward-regulation constraints in the local flexibility allocation problem. | Local allocation priorities under the Traffic Light Concept used in the formulation. | Objective of the local flexibility allocation problem. | Reducible-generator feasibility constraints in local allocation. | SESP scheduling of local flexible resources for the operation day. | SESP-operated local flexibility market serving DSO power-quality requirements. | Service scope of the presented local flexibility market. | Shiftable-profile load feasibility in local allocation. | Upward-regulation constraints in the local flexibility allocation problem.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-004","v141-b-g01-ev-006","v141-b-g01-ev-007","v141-b-g01-ev-010","v141-b-g01-ev-013","v141-b-g02-ev05","v141-b-g02-ev10","v141-b-g02-ev11","v141-b-g02-ev13","v141-b-g02-ev15","v141-b-g02-ev20","v141-b-g02-ev21","v141-b-g02-ev22","v141-b-g02-ev23","v141-b-g02-ev25","v141-b-g02-ev29","v141-b-g02-ev33","v141-b-g02-ev34","v141-b-g02-ev36","v141-b-g02-ev37","v141-b-g03-E13","v141-b-g03-E15","v141-b-g04-e03"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R003-E004","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"clearing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R003-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-010"]},"paper_scope_note":"There is direct basis for the DSO request, positive and negative regulation relative to the baseline, and SESP operational responsibility; the requested quantity must not be treated as actual supply quantity, nor cost management as the request reception interface."}}],"assertion_ids":["21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E004"]});
